## 12. Calibration: what "strong accept" rests on

The acceptance case: verbatim theme fit; three new closed-form results,
each with a falsifiable experiment; a memorable central law (`1 - 1/R_0`
for markets of models) that gives talks and reviews a handle; a complete
econ apparatus (externality, public good, policy triple); and validated
simulator ground truth to anchor it. The honest risks: reviewers who want
heterogeneous agents (answered as future work, and the secular-equation
machinery is stated to extend); and the dependence of Theorem 2's clean
form on the strong-correction limit (mitigated by reporting the exact
root). Nothing in the paper claims beyond what is derived or measured at
submission time.
